<!--
    The small notification icon.

    ⚠️ IT MUST BE A WHITE-ON-TRANSPARENT SILHOUETTE. Android masks this icon to
    a single colour from API 21 onwards; a full-colour logo comes out as a
    featureless grey square, which is the single most common "why does our
    notification look broken" complaint.

    A speech bubble rather than the AKN wordmark, for the same reason: at 24dp,
    masked to one colour, three letters are an unreadable smudge and a bubble is
    instantly legible. The maroon brand colour is applied by Android through
    default_notification_color in AndroidManifest.xml, so the brand is still
    there — as the tint.
-->
